{{also|BBL}}
==English==

===Etymology 1===
Modified from ''bl'' for ''barrel'' (b⸺l), reflecting a way of abbreviating that was used especially in previous centuries, wherein a doubled letter indicated plural count, as also with {{m|en|p.}}/page and {{m|en|pp.}}/pages and {{m|en|l.}}/line and {{m|en|ll.}}/lines; seen also in Spanish {{m|es|EE. UU.}}

